.Dd October 8, 2026
.Dt VSH 1
.Os UP-Term
.Sh NAME
.Nm vsh
.Nd the UP-Term shell, a POSIX shell for AmigaOS
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl i
.Op Fl s
.Nm
.Fl c Ar command
.Op Ar name Op Ar arg ...
.Nm
.Ar file
.Op Ar arg ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a POSIX shell with bash and zsh touches that runs AmigaDOS commands and
ixemul Unix programs alike.
It has pipes, the redirections
.Ql 2> 2>&1 &> <<EOF ,
.Ql $( ) ,
.Ql $(( )) ,
globs,
.Ic if , while , for
and
.Ic case ,
functions, aliases and job control
.Pf ( Ic jobs , fg , bg , wait ) .
Ctrl-C goes to the running command; Ctrl-Z suspends an ixemul program
(an AmigaDOS command cannot be stopped, and
.Nm
says so).
.Pp
There is no fork on the Amiga: subshells,
.Ql $( )
and all but the last stage of a pipeline run as processes of their own.
.Pp
Commands are looked for in
.Ev PATH ,
in Unix form as ixemul programs read it
.Pq Pa /UP-Term/bin:/gg/bin:/c No by default ,
then in the AmigaDOS Shell's path.
A name that starts with
.Ql /
means the parent directory when something is there, and otherwise what it
means on Unix:
.Pa /RAM/notes
is
.Pa RAM:notes ,
as ixemul programs name it.
.Pp
The
.Ic type
and
.Ic which
builtins shadow the AmigaDOS
.Ic C:Type
command, which stays reachable by its full name.
The
.Ic umask
builtin sets the local variable
.Ev UMASK ,
which the programs it starts inherit.
.Ss Options
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c Ar command
Run
.Ar command ;
.Ar name
becomes
.Li $0
and the
.Ar arg Ns s
the positional parameters.
.It Fl i
Interactive, also when the input is no console.
.It Fl s
Read commands from the standard input.
.El
.Ss Completion and keys
.Ic complete ,
.Ic compgen
and
.Ic compopt
work as in bash; Tab in an UP-Term window asks
.Nm
for the words.
.Ic bind
and an
.Pa .inputrc
.Pf ( Ev INPUTRC ,
else
.Pa $HOME/.inputrc )
set the window's line editor
.Pq Li set editing-mode vi | emacs .
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width INPUTRC
.It Ev HOME
The start directory and the place of
.Pa .vshrc ;
.Pa SYS:
when unset.
.It Ev PATH
Where commands are looked for, in Unix form.
.It Ev UMASK
The file mode mask the started programs take.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width ENVARC:vsh/vshrc
.It Pa ENVARC:vsh/vshrc
Read first at startup.
.It Pa $HOME/.vshrc
Read next.
.It Pa GG:bin/sh
.Nm
installed as
.Pa /gg/bin/sh ,
the shell ixemul programs run their commands with, when there is no Geek
Gadgets
.Pa GG: .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The status of the last command; an AmigaDOS return code (0, 5, 10, 20)
passes through.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ixkill 1 ,
.Xr upgetty 1 ,
.Xr UPTerm 1
.Pp
The kit's README.txt, section VSH, lists the differences from bash.
